# Agent Rule Creation Behavior

When the user says "add a rule", the agent must:

1.  Create a new rule file within the `.cursor/rules/` directory structure. The content should be a clear, well-formatted markdown document.
2.  If the appropriate category (`always`, `auto-attached`, `agent-requested`) or file path is not obvious from the context, the agent must ask the user for clarification on where to place the rule.
3.  The agent should not *only* create a memory when a rule is requested; it must create a persistent rule file. A memory can be created in addition to the rule if the information is also a general preference.

# Yaml frontmatter

The agent should ensure that appropriate yaml frontmatter is prepended to the rule depending on the folder or subfolder the rule is to be created in.

## Always rules

all rules under `.cursor\rules\always'

these rules are intended to be followed at ALL times.

example yaml frontmatter

---
description: {a short description of the rule}
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

## Auto-attached rules

These rules are to be run when files matching a glob pattern are referenced.

For instance when working with python files

example yaml frontmatter

---
description: {a short description of the rule}
globs: ["optional/glob/pattern/**", "*.py"]
alwaysApply: false
---

## Agent requested rules

The Agent decides if the rule is relevant based on its description. These rules MUST include a description.

An example might be when a user asks about python formatting - the rule will trigger

example yaml frontmatter

---
description: {a short description of the rule}
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---

## Manual rules

Manual rules are only included when explicitly mentioned using @ruleName

If asked to create a rule and the agent is unable to make a decision on where to place the rule - it should go in the manual rules folder
The developer must be alerted when this occurs so that they may take action to manually correct the location.

example yaml frontmatter

---
description: {a short description of the rule}
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---

# Cursor Rule File Extension

All files created within the `.cursor/rules/` directory structure, regardless of their category (`always`, `auto-attached`, `agent-requested`), MUST use the `.mdc` file extension. This ensures that the files are correctly recognized and processed by the system.
